  {
   "line": 7,
   "text": "Eight samples put the bins a thousand hertz apart, so every row tone lands in bin one. That spacing, eight thousand over N, is the frequency resolution. Close tones need a longer block. At forty samples, seven seventy and eight fifty-two share a bin. At two hundred and five, each tone gets its own bin, and an empty one on each side.",
   "clip": "/Users/cleiton.loiola/personal/dsp-lessons/12-dft/4-video/vo/line07.wav",
   "at": 76.78,
   "start": 76.78,
   "end": 92.78,
   "start_frame": 2303,
   "words": [
    {
     "word": "Eight",
